The three .typ files here are the Typst side of MiTeX, from https://github.com/mitex-rs/mitex
at commit f69eb43b52372e141b35661c049ce522567adbf0, path packages/mitex/specs/. That is the
commit the mitex 0.2.4 crate was published from, as its .cargo_vcs_info.json records. They
define the functions mitex's converter writes, such as mitexsqrt and textmath, in mitex-scope.

MiTeX is licensed under the Apache License 2.0, in LICENSE beside this file.

mod.typ and prelude.typ are unchanged. typst-0.15.patch holds every change to
latex/standard.typ, and applies to the upstream file with `patch -p1`:

- The import of @preview/xarrow, which is GPL-3.0-only and would be fetched from the network,
  is replaced by a one-line xarrow built on Typst's math.stretch.
- `kai`, which Typst 0.15 removed, is replaced by K in the KaTeX logo.
- angle.l and angle.r, which Typst 0.15 renamed, are chevron.l and chevron.r in \langle,
  \rangle, \lang, \rang and the bra-ket commands.
- \argmax and \argmin are written as operators, because Typst 0.15 has no argmax or argmin.
- Vmatrix's delimiter is the one character ‖, because Typst 0.15 takes no two-character
  delimiter "||".
- get-tex-color, which \color, \textcolor and \colorbox call, also takes #rrggbb, and panics
  on any other color that is not in mitex's color map, where upstream draws it uncolored.
  src/typeset.rs turns that panic into a scene error that names the color.

mitex's converter also writes 17 symbols by their names before Typst 0.15, and ignores any
command spec it is given in favour of its built-in one. src/typeset.rs renames those 17 in the
converter's output (TYPST_0_15_RENAMES), so the converter itself is not patched.

To upgrade mitex, fetch these files at the new crate's commit, reapply the patch, and run
`cargo test mitex_knows`, which names every command and environment that stops typesetting.
